      "created_at": "2025-11-04T13:00:18Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-11-04T13:01:31Z",
      "body": "> ```\r\n> $kbdtype = $(brightnessctl -l | grep -Po \"(?<=Device ')[^']*kbd_backlight[^']*(?=')\")\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> This will match any of the combinations above.\r\n\r\nI'd like this too, but the command returns nothing on my laptop (Tuxedo Infinitybook 14, gen 10).\r\n\r\n`brightnessctl -l` returns:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nAvailable devices:\r\nDevice 'amdgpu_bl1' of class 'backlight':\r\n        Current brightness: 18735 (30%)\r\n        Max brightness: 62451\r\n\r\nDevice 'input6::numlock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 1 (100%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'phy0-led' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 1 (100%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input12::mute' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 0 (0%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input6::scrolllock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 0 (0%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input3::numlock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 1 (100%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input3::capslock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 0 (0%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input3::scrolllock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 0 (0%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n\r\nDevice 'input6::capslock' of class 'leds':\r\n        Current brightness: 0 (0%)\r\n        Max brightness: 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo either it's not a generic solution, or I'm missing something in my installation.",
